How does Route 53 know about both ALBs?

You create two DNS records with the same name:

Record 1:
Name: myapp.com
Type: A
Alias: ON
Target: ALB-India

and

Record 2:
Name: myapp.com
Type: A
Alias: ON
Target: ALB-US

But you also configure a routing policy telling Route 53 when to use each ALB.

For example, with Failover routing:

myapp.com
   ↓
Route 53
   ↓
Primary ALB → India
   ↓
Health Check
   ↓
Healthy? ✅
   ↓
Send users here

If India becomes unhealthy:

myapp.com
   ↓
Route 53
   ↓
India ALB ❌
   ↓
US ALB ✅
   ↓
Send users to US
So the domain is not permanently pointing to only one ALB. Route 53 has both ALBs configured as possible destinations and chooses which one to return based on the routing policy.
In one sentence:
One domain can have multiple Route 53 records with the same name, and the routing policy determines which ALB the user is directed to.



